# Hi-Fi RUSH (PPSA17168) -- press past the title screen and the first-boot
# language/settings wizard.
#
# Anchors are wall-clock seconds from the FIRST PAD POLL, not from process
# start, so they are robust to how long the IoStore asset load takes. On a
# default launch the title screen ("Press Any Button") composites at roughly
# t=225 s of process time; the guest starts polling the pad well before that.
#
# Windows are 3 s wide because a range shorter than the interval between pad
# polls can be missed entirely (tools/AGENTS.md).
#
# Run with PROSPER_PAD_SCRIPT_LOG=1 so the route reports the transitions it
# actually delivered -- without it this route cannot tell "the guest ignored
# the input" from "the input was never applied".
#
# Cross is the confirm button everywhere observed so far: the title screen
# takes any button, and the language page's own prompt reads "(X) Next".

